# Neon Data API + Neon Auth — both PUBLIC by design (they're the browser's
# entry points, protected by RLS + the auth token, not by secrecy). Never
# put a Postgres connection string, a Meta token, or the svc_sync password
# in this file or anywhere under web/ — see web/README.md "Sécurité".
#
# IMPORTANT — URL trap, see web/README.md "Piège de l'URL Data API":
# these two variables come from DIFFERENT places in the Neon console and
# do NOT share a common URL. Use BOTH exactly as the console shows them —
# no stripping. (An earlier version of this file claimed the Data API URL
# needed ".apirest"/"/rest/v1" stripped off; that was wrong, disproven by
# direct curl testing against this SDK version — paste it as-is.)
#
# VITE_NEON_DATA_API_URL — Neon console > Data API > Connection details,
# used exactly as shown:
#   https://ep-xxx.apirest.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb/rest/v1
#
# VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL — Neon console > Auth tab, its OWN url, on a
# DIFFERENT subdomain label (".neonauth", not ".apirest") with a "/auth"
# suffix — also used exactly as shown:
#   https://ep-xxx.neonauth.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb/auth

VITE_NEON_DATA_API_URL=
VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=
